      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2014 The Royal College of Radiologists. Published by Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": "A duodenal diverticulum is a commonly encountered entity in gastrointestinal radiology with a wide variety of appearances. The purpose of this review is to describe the normal anatomy and embryology of the duodenum, discuss the differences between a true versus intraluminal duodenal diverticulum, and to highlight the normal appearance, potential complications, and imaging pitfalls of duodenal diverticula."
      },
